ption {:value "354505"} "Half-Lightweight (≤66 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "354580"} "Lightweight (≤73 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "354655"} "Half-Middleweight (≤81 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "354730"} "Middleweight (≤90 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "354805"} "Half-Heavyweight (≤100 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "354880"} "Heavyweight (&gt;100 kilograms), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "354922"} "Extra-Lightweight (≤48 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "354964"} "Half-Lightweight (≤52 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "355048"} "Half-Middleweight (≤63 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "355090"} "Middleweight (≤70 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "355132"} "Half-Heavyweight (≤78 kilograms), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "355174"} "Heavyweight (&gt;78 kilograms), Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "900513"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "17405"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "18158"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "18896"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "19625"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "260689"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "316309"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "18001298"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007178"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/352"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Lightweight (≤57 kilograms), Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} " 8 August 2016"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/902"} "Arena Carioca 2, Parque Olímpico da Barra, Barra da Tijuca, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/355006"} "23 from 23 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "At the Rio Olympics, women’s judo events provided some interesting and touching stories. The day after " [:a {:href "/athletes/121974"} "Majlinda Kelmendi"] " won the first gold medal for Kosovo, the young country torn by ethnic rivalries, " [:a {:href "/athletes/122491"} "Rafaela Silva"] " finally gained host country Brazil’s first gold medal, in the 57 kg class. But the main story behind Silva were her origins in the notorious favela (slum) " [:em {} "Cidade de Deus"] " (City of God) in Rio. It was there that the 2004 Olympic bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/33547"} "Flávio Canto"] " founded a martial arts school which was to turn Silva into the world’s top judoka in her class. The 24-year-old was not really a surprise victor as she was the 2013 World Champion and a two-time gold medalist at the Pan American Games. However, prior to the Olympics she had dropped to 14 in the rankings. Silva had competed in London 2012 where she was disqualified for an illegal leg grab against " [:a {:href "/athletes/125793"} "Hedvig Karakas"] " of Hungary. In Rio the two met again in the quarter-finals. This time, Silva scored a Waza-ari (half point) after 1:50 min, which proved to be sufficient to advance to the semi-final. After beating the second seed, Korean " [:a {:href "/athletes/124412"} "Kim Jan-Di"] ", earlier in the tournament, in the final Silva faced the top-seeded Asian Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/123511"} "Dorjsurengiin Sumiya"] ". Again, an early Waza-ari for a Sumi-otoshi (corner drop) was decisive in winning gold."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Bronze medals went to " [:a {:href "/athletes/106385"} "Telma Monteiro"] " of Portugal, a five-time European Champion, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/120792"} "Kaori Matsumoto"] " of Japan, the reigning Olympic and World Champion. Both were defeated by Sumiya in the quarter-finals and semi-finals, respectively, of the elimination round."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/122491"} "Rafaela Silva"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BRA.png"}] "BRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/123511"} "Dorjsürengiin Sumyaa"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/MGL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/MGL.png"}] "MGL"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/106385"} "Telma Monteiro"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POR.png"}] "POR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/120792"} "Kaori Matsumoto"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/121250"} "Corina Căprioriu"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROU.png"}] "ROU"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=5"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/131858"} "Lien Chen-Ling"]]